(2304157, 315140, 30807, '<td valign="top">The trees bend as if refracted, but it is reflection, I think. I suspect the light of the sunset is refracted however, so you have capture two ''refractions'' in the one image - well done<br/> <br/>I Love the image though - we have just that light in Shropshire, here in England. It takes me back 50 years to childhood summer dusk at the local lake<br/> <br/>Good luck with your image</td>', 'The trees bend as if refracted, but it is reflection, I think. I suspect the light of the sunset is refracted however, so you have capture two ''refractions'' in the one image - well done I Love the image though - we have just that light in Shropshire, here in England. It takes me back 50 years to childhood summer dusk at the local lake Good luck with your image', '2006-04-11 17:46:48.000000', NULL, 1),
(2304160, 316308, 30807, '<td valign="top">Looking like a splash of light, part of a tulip caught by the sun, or a wipe of smoke coming from a spinning vortex, I find this image of the top of a wineglass stem quite a surprise. I like the red and green in the background just under the bowl, and the curious smokey look very intriguing. <br/> <br/>Wishing you well with your photo</td>', 'Looking like a splash of light, part of a tulip caught by the sun, or a wipe of smoke coming from a spinning vortex, I find this image of the top of a wineglass stem quite a surprise. I like the red and green in the background just under the bowl, and the curious smokey look very intriguing.  Wishing you well with your photo', '2006-04-11 17:49:56.000000', NULL, 1),
