(2306593, 316703, 38032, '<td valign="top">I had you this as my top pic.  The effort, beauty  and intrigue here really should have given it a ribbon.  You should sell it as a print (not sure if people buy prints but it definitely would have interest on a wall.<br/>Looking at it closely I can see that noise and sharpness could use adjustment -- that''s probably what pushed it down a bit - I''m not a purist like that though ... I''m more about ideas and wow-factor when it comes to voting..<br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2006-04-12 10:52:13.</i></td>', 'I had you this as my top pic.  The effort, beauty  and intrigue here really should have given it a ribbon.  You should sell it as a print (not sure if people buy prints but it definitely would have interest on a wall.Looking at it closely I can see that noise and sharpness could use adjustment -- that''s probably what pushed it down a bit - I''m not a purist like that though ... I''m more about ideas and wow-factor when it comes to voting..', '2006-04-12 11:49:46.000000', '2006-04-12 11:52:13.000000', 0),
(2306606, 316703, 36382, '<td valign="top">Thank you metatate.  I am a bit mad at myself for not doing a better job with this picture in post processing.  I kinda rushed it and somehow added all this grain.  Funny cos I spent about three days perfecting the drops and taking the picture, then rushed the end.  I love the effect though and definitely want to explore it some more.  Thanks too for the link to Chuck Close.  I checked him out and found his work inspirational.</td>', 'Thank you metatate.  I am a bit mad at myself for not doing a better job with this picture in post processing.  I kinda rushed it and somehow added all this grain.  Funny cos I spent about three days perfecting the drops and taking the picture, then rushed the end.  I love the effect though and definitely want to explore it some more.  Thanks too for the link to Chuck Close.  I checked him out and found his work inspirational.', '2006-04-12 11:54:05.000000', NULL, 0),
